I found the issue! Look at lines 698-702:

```swift
case .startThread(let highlightId):
    // Provider configuration check will happen in ThreadPanel
    guard threadState.isConfigured else {
        return
    }
```

If the provider is not configured, the function just returns silently with NO ERROR MESSAGE to the user. That's why the Annotate button appears to do nothing!

Additionally, the check on line 700 is `threadState.isConfigured` which checks if there's an active provider. Let me verify that this is working correctly by checking the AIProviderManager.

